<header class="desk-intro" data-workspace="word-to-wordpress">
<p class="eyebrow">Free Word document preparation</p>
<h1>Word to WordPress converter</h1>
<p>Bring your .docx draft. Preview the conversion, review the article, then take editable blocks into a new WordPress post.</p>
<nav class="desk-start" aria-label="Convert Word to WordPress"><button id="start-word-file" type="button" class="button">1. Choose a Word document</button><button id="start-review" type="button" class="secondary">2. Review the article</button><button id="start-handoff" type="button" class="secondary">3. Take WordPress blocks</button></nav>
<p class="small">No account, upload, plugin, or API credits. Plain .docx files up to 8 MiB. Common headings, emphasis, lists, web links, and simple tables can be kept. Images become placeholders; review every omission before applying.</p>
<p id="sample" class="small">Try the editor and exports first: <button id="start-sample" type="button" class="secondary">Try a fictional sample</button> This sample is prewritten, not a Word-file import.</p>
